 "figures": {
  "fighting": {
   "title": "How much changes hands",
   "caption": "One line per world, means over 50 iterations.",
   "recipe": "**Runs.** Pilot worlds of `research/oee/pilots/run.py` in the engine's own code, kept in `GraphOfLifeRuns/.pilots/S`, two seeds each, at 10,000 tokens for 1,000 iterations with a whole world every 100: B2 without revolutions (`--set hidden_layers=16 message_amount=8 message_prepass=false allow_handover=false mutate_on_replication=true incumbency=1.5 birth_links=2 mend_on_death=true prune_needs=2 valence=8 keep_home=0.3 max_age=100 min_child=10 allow_revolutions=false --proto engine=true`, worlds `S1-norev`), the same with a lottery contest (`contest=lottery`, `G1-lottery`), with stakes pooled by genotype (`pool=genotype`, `G2-genotype`), with only the sense of which neighbours carry one's own brain (`kin_sense=true`, `G3-kinsense`), and with family tags (`tag_rate=0.05`) sensed (`kin_sense=true`, `G4-familysense`) or pooled (`pool=family`, `G5-familypool`).\n\n**Data.** From each world's `series.jsonl`.\n\n1. Count the nodes whose winner was not their owner in each game, per 100 agents.\n\n**To make it again:** `python3 book_figures.py games`."
  },
  "groups": {
   "title": "How large a group of clones is",
   "caption": "One line per world, every 10th iteration: the agents of an agent's connected group of neighbours with the same brain, averaged over agents.",
   "recipe": "**Runs.** Pilot worlds of `research/oee/pilots/run.py` in the engine's own code, kept in `GraphOfLifeRuns/.pilots/S`, two seeds each, at 10,000 tokens for 1,000 iterations with a whole world every 100: B2 without revolutions (`--set hidden_layers=16 message_amount=8 message_prepass=false allow_handover=false mutate_on_replication=true incumbency=1.5 birth_links=2 mend_on_death=true prune_needs=2 valence=8 keep_home=0.3 max_age=100 min_child=10 allow_revolutions=false --proto engine=true`, worlds `S1-norev`), the same with a lottery contest (`contest=lottery`, `G1-lottery`), with stakes pooled by genotype (`pool=genotype`, `G2-genotype`), with only the sense of which neighbours carry one's own brain (`kin_sense=true`, `G3-kinsense`), and with family tags (`tag_rate=0.05`) sensed (`kin_sense=true`, `G4-familysense`) or pooled (`pool=family`, `G5-familypool`).\n\n**Data.** From each world's `series.jsonl`.\n\n1. Every 10th iteration, join neighbours with the same brain and take the size of each agent's group, averaged over agents (`organisation`, `cloneMean`).\n\n**To make it again:** `python3 book_figures.py games`."
  },
  "elo": {
   "title": "How much better than the founders",
   "caption": "One line per world, its eras played against each other, four contests per pair.",
   "recipe": "**Runs.** Pilot worlds of `research/oee/pilots/run.py` in the engine's own code, kept in `GraphOfLifeRuns/.pilots/S`, two seeds each, at 10,000 tokens for 1,000 iterations with a whole world every 100: B2 without revolutions (`--set hidden_layers=16 message_amount=8 message_prepass=false allow_handover=false mutate_on_replication=true incumbency=1.5 birth_links=2 mend_on_death=true prune_needs=2 valence=8 keep_home=0.3 max_age=100 min_child=10 allow_revolutions=false --proto engine=true`, worlds `S1-norev`), the same with a lottery contest (`contest=lottery`, `G1-lottery`), with stakes pooled by genotype (`pool=genotype`, `G2-genotype`), with only the sense of which neighbours carry one's own brain (`kin_sense=true`, `G3-kinsense`), and with family tags (`tag_rate=0.05`) sensed (`kin_sense=true`, `G4-familysense`) or pooled (`pool=family`, `G5-familypool`).\n\n**Data.** From each world's checkpoints, `ckpt_<iteration>.npz`.\n\n1. For every pair of the eras 0, 100, 200, 500 and 1,000 play four contests, two in each era's world: every agent gets a brain drawn at random from one era or the other, mutation is switched off, and 20 iterations are played under the world's own rules (`research/oee/pilots/tourney.py --T 20 --reps 2`).\n2. Fit one rating per era (Bradley\u2013Terry, `research/oee/pilots/elo.py`), the founders at 0.\n\n**To make it again:** `python3 book_figures.py games`."
  }
 }
}
